From b9437499052136f4f0c3bc15c45aedeeb210d4d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicholas Hemsley <nick.hems@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Feb 2026 17:27:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add Focused Context Mode for agent threads

Adds a 'Focused Context Mode' feature that limits conversation context
sent to the LLM to only recent messages, enabling longer conversations
without hitting context limits.

Features:
- Toggle button in thread view to enable/disable mode
- Interactive slider to adjust number of recent messages
- Visual histogram showing message distribution (user/agent colors)
- Click histogram bars to adjust window, Ctrl+click to also scroll
- Auto-caps at configurable limit (default 100) when first enabled
- Persists mode and message count per thread in database

Implementation:
- AcpThread manages focused_context_mode state and num_messages
- Thread applies windowing in build_request_messages()
- AgentConnection trait notifies backends of mode changes
- New FocusedContextPanel with slider and histogram visualization
- Settings: focused_context_message_limit (default 100)

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
